# English only inside the project

Everything that becomes part of this codebase must be written in English:

- Code identifiers (variables, functions, classes, files, folders)
- Code comments and JSDoc/TSDoc
- Commit messages, branch names, PR titles/descriptions
- Seed/fixture data (e.g. menu categories, dish names, user emails)
- Config files, `README.md`, docs, `.mdc` rules
- UI copy/labels in the apps (`customer-web`, `staff-web`), unless a task
  explicitly asks for localized/multi-language content

This applies regardless of what language the conversation with the user is
happening in (chat responses to the user may be in another language per the
user's own preference — that does not change this rule for anything written
into the repo).

If existing content violates this (leftover Cyrillic strings, mixed-language
seed data, etc.), flag it and prefer fixing it over adding more of the same.
